<%# locals: (id:, title:, state: :idle, summary: nil) %>
<%# HQ accordion section (plan-approved pattern; Ember
    port/components/hq-shift-manage-section.hbs over UiSection). DaisyUI
    collapse via native details/summary.

    Guided flow: only the :current section renders open, so the operator faces
    one decision at a time. Every other section collapses to a one-line status
    row — the summary local says what is outstanding there, so nothing is
    hidden, only folded. Any row is one tap away for out-of-order requests
    (a walk-up pog), and the hq-shift controller re-opens and scrolls to a
    section for the checkout choreography.

    The "you are here" spotlight rides Tailwind's open:/group-open: variants
    rather than the server-rendered state, so it follows the section the
    operator is actually looking at — including one the controller folded mid
    turbo-stream, or one they opened by hand. A snapshot class would keep
    claiming "you are here" on a section that had since closed.

    Emphasis is border colour, never a background tint: an area tint reads as a
    loud slab in dark mode, while a border reads the same in both themes. The
    summary badge (not a separate marker icon) carries what is outstanding, so
    there is one source of truth to keep fresh — see the summary streams in
    Hq::ShiftManageController. %>
<%
  border = state == :attention ? "border-warning" : "border-base-300"
  surface = state == :complete ? "bg-base-200" : "bg-base-100"
  section_class = "collapse collapse-arrow group mb-4 border #{border} #{surface} " \
                  "open:border-primary"
%>
<details id="<%= id %>" data-hq-section <%= "open" if state == :current %>
         class="<%= section_class %>">
  <summary class="collapse-title min-h-9 text-lg font-semibold text-heading cursor-pointer">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1 pe-6">
       <span class="hidden group-open:inline text-primary">
        <%= fa_icon "arrow-right", :solid %>
      </span>
      <span><%= title %></span>
      <% if summary.present? %>
        <%# lg:ms-auto, not ms-auto: once the row wraps on a narrow screen the
            summary lands on its own line, where pushing it to the far edge
            strands it away from the title it belongs to. %>
        <span class="ms-2 font-semibold text-lg">&bullet; <%= summary %></span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </summary>
  <div class="collapse-content">
    <%= yield %>
  </div>
</details>
